{
  "id": "30737_kinen",
  "headword": "{祈念|きねん}",
  "reading": "きねん",
  "romaji": "kinen",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "prayer; wish; supplication",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "prayer; earnest wish",
      "explanation": "Praying or wishing earnestly for something good to come about. Formal, and used above all for public, collective wishes such as peace, safety, or recovery."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30737_kinen_ex1",
      "japanese": "{平和|へいわ}を{祈念|きねん}する。",
      "english": "To pray for peace.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30737_kinen_ex2",
      "japanese": "{皆様|みなさま}のご{健康|けんこう}を{祈念|きねん}いたします。",
      "english": "I pray for everyone's good health.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30737_kinen_ex3",
      "japanese": "{式典|しきてん}では{被災地|ひさいち}の{一日|いちにち}も{早|はや}い{復興|ふっこう}が{祈念|きねん}された。",
      "english": "At the ceremony, prayers were offered for the earliest possible recovery of the disaster-stricken area.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Do not confuse with its homophone {記念|きねん} (commemoration), which is far more common. The two appear side by side in names such as {平和|へいわ}{祈念|きねん}{像|ぞう} (Peace Prayer Statue) versus {記念|きねん}{館|かん} (memorial hall).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {平和|へいわ}を{祈念|きねん}する: to pray for peace\n- ご{多幸|たこう}を{祈念|きねん}{申|もう}し{上|あ}げます: I wish you every happiness (set closing phrase)\n- {安全|あんぜん}{祈念|きねん}: prayer for safety\n- {祈念|きねん}{式典|しきてん}: a memorial prayer ceremony\n\nREGISTER:\nWritten and ceremonial. In speech, ordinary people say {祈|いの}る; {祈念|きねん}する belongs to speeches, formal letters, and ceremonies.",
